<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Date Harumune</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1578">1578</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Date Harumune was a Japanese warlord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> and head of the Date clan of southern Mutsu. From 1542 he fought his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-tanemune">Date Tanemune</a> in the Tenbun war, a conflict that drew in many neighbouring families; he won by 1548 and moved the clan's seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonezawa">Yonezawa</a>. He was the grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/date-masamune">Date Masamune</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/date-harumune.jpg" alt="Date Harumune" width="320" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Date_Harumune.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
